Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(ballz): the recovered ball, the title screen, and
 the 3-2-1-GO start

- BallShell/BallCtrl/BallFire vendored verbatim from the legacy tvm-catalog
  as curated mesh-json assets; the FireArrow texture on the inner controller
  ball IS the aim indicator, as the original had it
- steering: jump input (Space hops straight up, own jumpImpulse tuning),
  full-position arrow anchoring + arrowLift (the aim rides the ball centre)
- mouse: HOLD to roll toward the pointer (aim = pointer, accelerator = held
  button); click/drag-kick scheme removed
- BallZ hero card on the Games shelf -> title screen (ballz-menu.ts) with
  Start Game + course roster; game courses leave the generic level list
- race start: 3-2-1-GO overlay, controls locked until GO (except paused
  worlds - harnesses are never held by presentation), rules.reset at GO;
  cancels on any programmatic activity; revision baseline at first tick
  (mount runs inside world.loaded, before create() bumps revision)
- smokes updated and green: ballz (recovered-model assertions), games
  (hero -> menu -> countdown -> play ceremony)
